+## 2026-09-22 — session 59: clean 6.18.52 boot, and the i686 boot-size gap gets a number
+
+<!-- src: engineering/FOLLOWUP-2026-09-22-kernel-boot-and-i686-boot-size.md -->
+
+**Kernel**: `build_kernel_vm.sh` on linux-cachymod-6.18.52 (28/28 patches) →
+`SUCCESS in 1798s`, bzImage 5071872 B, `setup _end=29552` (gate ok), every
+link by lccc-ld. `qemu_boot_test.sh` **16/16**, and — unlike session 58 —
+the serial log has **zero** `WARNING`/`Call Trace`/ACPI errors. The
+`free_large_kmalloc` warning session 58 left open did **not** reproduce, and
+neither did its trigger (`Failure resolving symbol`, `AE_AML`); with
+SeaBIOS `1.16.3-debian` here, "not triggered" is not "fixed" — the gdbstub
+probe still owes an answer.
+
+**Measured the i686 boot-size gap instead of guessing at it.** New
+`scripts/boot_insn_census.py`: over 21 `arch/x86/boot` TUs on identical
+command lines lccc emits **5127 instructions vs gcc's 3183 (+61.1 %)**;
+`movl` alone is +1176 of the +1944. The structural counters name the cause:
+**546 store-to-frame-slot vs gcc's 41**, 342 vs 61 loads back, and **70 of
+70 functions open a frame where gcc opens 30 of 67** (2408 more frame
+bytes). `LCCC_DBG_RA` on `check_cpuflags` shows `values=22 assigned=10` with
+short-lived values marked `elig=true` still given slots. This is
+`subsystems/i686.md` §2.2 with a corpus-wide number on it.
+
+**Falsified** the obvious fix: the i686 "immediately-consumed values get no
+home" policy (`prologue.rs`) looks like the cause of those round trips, and
+its stated premise — a home only costs a `movl %R,%eax` relay — is false for
+the ops `try_emit_int_binop_direct` reads in place. Made it a switch
+(`CCC_NO_I686_ACCUM_NOHOME`) and measured: **+391 B on the boot corpus, 17
+of 20 objects worse**. The policy stays; the switch stays so nobody
+re-derives this. Do-not-retry.
+
+**Landed** `fold_copy_narrow_ext_pairs`: `movl %S,%D` + `movX{l,w}l
+%D<narrow>,%D` → one `movX{l,w}l %S<narrow>,%D` (45 `movzwl %ax,%eax` sites
+in the boot corpus alone). Boot object sum **−104 B**, gate `_end`
+**28144 → 28048** paired, i686 regression corpus **−154 B (-Os)** /
+**−434 B (-O2)**. Guarded by three tests, one of which routes the peephole's
+output through `i686::assembler::assemble` — because the pass shipped
+emitting `movzwl%bx` (a `trim_end`'d mnemonic with no space restored), which
+**passed every text assertion** (the classifier files an unparseable line
+under its `Other` catch-all) and only died when eight boot TUs were really
+compiled. Mutation-checked: removing the space fails that test alone.
+
+**Two measurement traps, both now written down.** (1) The boot gate moves
+**3120 B** between tree states (before vs after a full `build_kernel_vm.sh`,
+via `ensure_boot_offset_stubs` re-stubbing `zoffset.h`/`voffset.h`, which
+also decides whether `.pecompat` exists) — a gate number is worthless
+unpaired. (2) `gcc-multilib`/`libc6-dev-i386` were absent, so every `-m32`
+regression test **skipped**; installing them moved the suite
+**737/0/8 → 742/0/8**. An i686 claim from a host without multilib is worth
+nothing.
+
+**Validation**: `cargo test --lib` **3111/0/7**; `run_regression_suite.sh`
+**742/0/8**, AB-diff 0; boot gate PASS (`.text` 20335 → 20329);
