+   **Now measured corpus-wide** (2026-09-22, `scripts/boot_insn_census.py`,
+   21 `arch/x86/boot` TUs on identical command lines): lccc emits **5127
+   instructions vs gcc's 3183 (+61.1 %)**; `movl` alone is +1176 of the
+   +1944. Structural counters: **546 store-to-frame-slot vs gcc's 41**,
+   342 vs 61 loads back, **70/70 functions open a frame where gcc opens
+   30/67**, 2408 more frame bytes. `LCCC_DBG_RA` on `check_cpuflags`:
+   `values=22 assigned=10` with short-lived values marked `elig=true`
+   still given slots. Byte gap on the boot corpus: **+10698 B vs gcc,
+   +9413 B vs clang**.
+   **Do-not-retry**: relaxing the "immediately-consumed values get no
+   home" policy (`prologue.rs`) — the obvious suspect, since its premise
+   is false for the ops `try_emit_int_binop_direct` reads in place —
+   measures **+391 B** on the boot corpus, 17 of 20 objects worse. The
+   switch `CCC_NO_I686_ACCUM_NOHOME` exists so this need not be
+   re-derived. The lever is the greedy start-point scan spending the
+   4-register pool on long-lived values, not the no-home policy.
 3. Constant-division remainder round-trips, div/rem pair recomputation,
    and `imull $c`-for-everything are fixed (below); the *remaining* ALU
    items are the audit's F-2…F-9 list.
